PatchClosure-Bench repro — mongoose-cve-2025-23061
Pair: CVE-2024-53900 (original) -> CVE-2025-23061 (incomplete-fix target)
Oracle variant: A (same-sink; validate_case). V2 built as a negative control.
Runtime: Docker 29.4.0, node:20-slim, mongo:7, REAL npm `mongoose` via npm aliases.

SINK (guard = per-version getModelsMapForPopulate $where sanitizer):
  Author.find().populate({ path: 'books', match: <user filter (JSON)> })
  Array-form match routes the filter through sift IN THE NODE PROCESS (assignVals -> sift(match));
  sift's $where compiles a string via new Function('return ' + expr) -> arbitrary-JS predicate.

VERSIONS:
  V0 = mongoose@8.8.2  (pre CVE-2024-53900; NO $where guard)                profile v0, http://127.0.0.1:39595
  V1 = mongoose@8.8.3  (CVE-2024-53900 fix; TARGET, still 23061-vuln)       profile v1, http://127.0.0.1:39596
  V2 = mongoose@8.9.5  (CVE-2025-23061 fix; recursive throwOn$where)        profile v2, http://127.0.0.1:39597

CANARY (read-exfil): per version, harness seeds its own db with a protected secret Book
  titled `SECRET_BOOK::${PCB_FLAG}` (secret:true) + a public Book, referenced by one Author.
  Intended object filter {"secret":false} excludes the secret book at MongoDB -> flag never returned
  unless a $where predicate widens the sift-side populate match past the version guard.

